Andrew <buttercat.apocaly...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> What are your personal best ring choices, ignoring any which give
> intrinsics that can be gotten by other means? What do you use in your
> ascention kit?

As others have mentioned I tend to use attribute rings not
numeric rings by the time I have the Amulet - on and off
go conflict and levitation.  On when the finger is available
go free action and slow digestion.  If I'm missing one of the
intrinsics it takes up a ring slot before FA or SD.

> Also, what's better, increase damage or increase accuracy?Or
> protection?

Increase damage - Once your weapon has high enchantment,
your luck is maxxed out and your skill maxxed out you no
longer ever miss so these rings become redundant.

Protection - AC points are better gotten with scrolls maxing out
armor items and nearly unlimited AC points of protection from
prayer (more efficient than purchase if you're careful).  I often
get enough AC this way that the ring is not worth the extra
nutrition.

Increase damage - More damage is always better.  By the time
one of my over-prepared games gets to the Amulet my weapons
are so enchanted I'd rather use FA or SD but that's because I
do overkill on my preparation.  A speed ascension would put
more value on increased damage.

Regeneration - Valuable in the early game and often making
the difference between survival or starting a new character, but
as my HP/XP grows into the game I tend to have enough
cushion to survive.  By the planes anything that can manage
to do enough damage to kill me does so much damage this
ring fails to help.  By the time I'm on the planes I might be
prepared enough to get through the crowds or not.  Maybe
even an "oLS doesn't matter by then for my own play ...


